{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912092-anchor-on-theme-distant-cousins-and-missing-links-forum-game","id":912092,"title":"Anchor On Theme: Distant Cousins and Missing Links [Forum Game]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-10T22:12:34-07:00","id":912092,"title":"Anchor On Theme: Distant Cousins and Missing Links [Forum Game]","content":"One of the things I find nifty about Beast's approach to crossover is how having your character be a common link between some number of other supernatural beings through brood Lairs or shared Family Ties by design helps your character become more like a common link between those particular supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> One of the implications behind the Begotten treating pretty much every supernatural being as kin is that with a little legwork you can make connections between any given pair of monsters if you can figure out the kind of Horror, Lair, or person that would bridge the gap between characters who otherwise might not interact.<br /> <br /> So the name of the game is this: make a character that a Beast could claim Kinship with, based on some thematic element of a previous poster's character \u2014 could be a shared haunting ground, a favored feeding method, basic ideological compatibility, you name it.<br /> <br /> This is set up a little differently than similar games in that you don't necessarily have to make one character per post or link them to the post immediately above yours \u2014 &quot;no neat little boxes&quot; is, after all, part of Beast's themes, and there's nothing in the arrangement that requires a strict two-character connection (and lord knows I've seen simul-postings throw things out of whack often enough) \u2014 but for ease of navigation it'd be preferable to quote or at least name the character you're tying your monster(s) to.<br /> <br /> Three examples to start things off:<br /> <br /> <b>Piebald Maggie</b> becomes strangely fixated on random objects every so often, as might be expected of a changeling whose Clarity is tenuous at the best of times, but the cluster of folklore and superstitions that guides her approach to collection is perhaps the greater problem. She's been stealing junk for over a decade now, and that the safest place she can think to keep the massive pile of trinkets is a clearing in the Hedge would be worrying even if she weren't possessed of the unshakeable sense that she is building something.<br /> <br /> <b>Whistler</b> was always fascinated by birds, which is hardly surprising for a Raptor, but his Horror seldom takes to the skies. More for him are the grasping branches of the deep woods and the thrashing prey of butcher-birds and hanging-trees. He's a sucker for the birdsong from which he got his nickname, but he's been trying to avoid entangling the local orchestra in his hunts; he's a big believer in the whole &quot;music soothes the savage beast&quot; rigmarole and he's not quite ready to give up that comfort in the name of a simple meal.<br /> <br /> Nobody's given much consideration to <b>Number Twelve</b> since its existence was wiped from the public record thirty years ago, but the strangled ghost of the orchestra pit still plagues the actor's guild at the local theater even as repeated banishment to the Underworld flays its identity down to lingering resentment for the amateur necromancer that bound them beneath the stage. It knows that the source of its misery is hidden among the troupe, but the vestiges of humanity that stop it from simply killing every player are wearing thin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T22:26:08-07:00","id":912102,"title":"","content":"<b>Silas McCoy</b> killed himself for a reason he now finds utterly ridiculous. The self-proclaimed cultural critic has decided to help ghosts pass on until he finds something better to do, like pick up the momentos the dead leave behind. Those are nice. In general it's nice to be able to get a living out of all of this, all the death and loneliness. He could have done a lot worse. Having a purpose means not worrying about things like what people think of you. A lot worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:42:15-07:00","id":912352,"title":"","content":"<b>Ladon</b> watched as their mentor was consumed by the investments of an Acamoth. They didn't need the hard sell into the Fangs of Mara. Now the mage that named themself after the hundred-headed, never-sleeping dragon roams nightmarish dream-scapes and explores phobias as they work towards the grand plan of their Legacy; to infiltrate the nightmares of one of the greatest of the Abyssal intruders, and there find a way to kill it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:25:40-07:00","id":912434,"title":"","content":"<b>The Owner</b> has little aside from his antique shop, but that doesn't bother him. He specializes in acquiring and disseminating &quot;special&quot; accessories. Making sure they stay in circulation is a full-time job. He is vaguely aware that his trusted assistant appears different every time he looks, but it's more than he can say about the patrons. He can never quite see their faces, or even them at all - just little winded springs of potential. All he knows is what to say and which wares to give them to release this potential. After it's done, the pieces often find their way back on his shelves. Occasionally they need to be stolen from evidence lockers first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:42:09-07:00","id":985689,"title":"","content":"<b>Amelia Cobblestone</b> was a founding member of the pack of Iron Masters that concerns itself with the city's historical district, and she gives particular attention to the movements of her block's various instrument-Claimed buskers. She's had to stop them from drawing mortals toward the old locus behind the pawn shop once or twice, but for the moment she keeps her hand in on the Siskur-Dah by using that same font of wind-Essence to hunt down thieving spirits in the district's Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}